  "provenance_note": "New, separately dated baseline succeeding the untouched 2026-08-17 activation baseline after the first paper-active session exposed an alpaca-py SDK compatibility defect. Tier 1 is byte-identical. Exactly two Tier-2 files changed: live_slc/execution.py now unwraps broker enum objects through their .value before every order-status decision, fixing real OrderStatus.FILLED/CANCELED/ACCEPTED handling in polling, cancellation, flatten confirmation, target verification, and degraded-position recovery; live_slc/run_slc_live.py uses that shared normalization throughout, persists the broker order ID immediately after acceptance, records actual fill/notional/risk/slippage data, counts idempotent position opens/closes and realized session P&L, records partial-fill degradation through the existing critical audit path, and counts persisted acted-on signals rather than only happy-path result counters. The incident and broker-confirmed reconciliation are documented in research/slc_paper_incident_20260818_nvda.md. No frozen signal, market-structure, zone, stochastic, entry, stop, target, ranking, sizing, or numeric risk rule changed.",
